  "id": "nest-building",
  "term": "nest building",
  "definition": "Nest building is a construction behavior in birds in which they make nests using particular materials, structures, and locations. In learning research, it is used to study social learning, conformity, and the development of behavioral traditions because birds can learn nest-building choices from others.",
